    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "<|channel>thought\n<channel|>But it doesn't feel like \"healing\" matters. When I look at the people who were supposed to be there... the ones who didn't make it... it just feels like I'm holding onto a spot that belongs to them. Like I'm just a placeholder. It feels so wrong to even be breathing when they aren't. It feels like a debt I can't pay back.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "That feeling of being a placeholder for someone else is incredibly heavy, but it's a sign that your mind is trying to protect you from the pain of loss rather than a sign that you don't belong. You are not a debt; you are a life that has been unfairly interrupted, and the guilt you feel is just the weight of grief trying to convince you that your existence is an error. It is okay to feel like this, and it is okay to let go of the impossible expectation that you must fill a space that was never yours to begin with.",
      "source": "target",
